Calculation of Theoretical Output Thrust of Double-Acting Single Piston Rod Hydraulic Cylinder in Differential Circuit.
Note: The "theoretical output force" stipulated in JB/T10205-2010 refers to the theoretical output thrust of the cylinder under the nominal pressure value (or within the range) including a nominal pressure value. Strictly speaking, if the above formula is calculated using nominal pressure, it should be the theoretical output thrust of the cylinder under this nominal pressure value.

(2) Calculation Formula for Cylinder Motion Resistance
The actual output force of the cylinder is less than the theoretical output force of the cylinder, because the resistance caused by back pressure, friction, and the influence of leakage is ignored when calculating the theoretical output force of the cylinder. The calculation formula for cylinder motion resistance is
F=F1+F2+F3±F4±F5 (2-4)
where F——Total resistance of cylinder motion, or all external loads converted to the piston (piston rod), in N;
F1——External load resistance including external friction force, mainly composed of the friction resistance of moving parts connected to the cylinder and the reaction force of the driven external load, with a value equal to the actual output force of the cylinder, in N;
F2——Friction resistance of the sealing device or system of the hydraulic cylinder, generally estimated as 4% of the theoretical output force of the cylinder, in N;
F3——Resistance caused by back pressure, including the buffering pressure generated when the hydraulic cylinder with buffer enters the buffering state, in N;
F4——The gravity of the cylinder and the moving parts connected to the cylinder, converted to the cylinder axis line, in formula (2-4), when the gravity is opposite to the direction of motion, take "+", when the gravity is the same as the direction of motion, take "-", F4=mg, in N;
F5——When the hydraulic cylinder starts, brakes or changes direction, the inertia resistance of the cylinder and the moving parts connected to the cylinder, converted to the piston (piston rod), in formula (1-4), when accelerating and starting, take "+", when decelerating and braking, take "-", F5=ma, in N;
m——Mass of the cylinder and the moving parts connected to the cylinder, converted to the piston (piston rod), in kg;
g——Acceleration of gravity, gn=9.80665 m/s2;
a——Acceleration, uniform motion a=0, in m/s2.
Note: The formula m=F4/gn can be used to obtain the mass of the cylinder and the moving parts connected to the cylinder, converted to the piston (piston rod).

(3) Calculation Formula for Cylinder Running Speed
1) For double-acting single piston rod hydraulic cylinder, the calculation formula for cylinder process speed is
v1=Q/(60A1)×10^6 (2-5)
where v1——Process speed of double-acting single piston rod hydraulic cylinder, in mm/s;
Q——Input flow rate of the rodless chamber, in L/min;
A1——Effective area of the rodless chamber, A1=πD^2/4, in mm^2;
D——Cylinder (inner) diameter, in mm.
The calculation formula for cylinder return speed is
v2=Q/(60A2)×10^6 (2-6)
where v2——Return speed of double-acting single piston rod hydraulic cylinder, in mm/s;
Q——Input flow rate of the rod chamber, in L/min;
A2——Effective area of the rod chamber, A2=π(D^2-d^2)/4, in mm^2;
D——Cylinder (inner) diameter, in mm;
d——Piston rod diameter, in mm.
2) For single-acting plunger hydraulic cylinder, the calculation formula for cylinder process speed is
v3=Q/(60A3)×10^6 (2-7)
where v3——Process speed of single-acting plunger hydraulic cylinder, in mm/s;
Q——Input flow rate of the working chamber, in L/min;
A3——Cross-sectional area of the piston rod, A3=πd^2/4, in mm^2;
d——Piston rod diameter, in mm.
Formula (2-7) is applicable to the calculation of the process speed of the double-acting single piston rod hydraulic cylinder in the differential circuit with the plunger cylinder or the hydraulic cylinder as the executing element.
(4) Calculation Formula for Speed Ratio of Reciprocating Motion of Double-Acting Single Piston Rod Hydraulic Cylinder
The calculation formula for speed ratio is
φ=v1/v2=(D^2-d^2)/D^2=1/σ (2-8)
where φ——Ratio of process speed to return speed of double-acting single piston rod hydraulic cylinder, referred to as speed ratio;
σ——Area ratio of two chambers, σ=A1/A2=πD^2/4/(π(D^2-d^2)/4);
A1——Effective area of the rodless chamber, in mm^2;
A2——Effective area of the rod chamber, in mm^2;
D——Cylinder (inner) diameter, in mm;
